this came up when a hacker tried to genocide cats using an uncursed
scroll of genocide.  his kitten later grew into a housecat and promptly
died.  the correct behavior here should be that genociding cats
kills all "cats" immediately.  it raises an interesting tangential
issue: monsters should be allowed to range in experience from level 1
to whatever is appropriate for that monster type (but i'd just as soon
have the upper limit be 30 as it is for the player).  i don't know what
would happen if you encountered a level 25 gelatinous cube but meeting
an "ancient" level 30 dragon should be a nightmare.  a "baby" dragon,
let's say less than level 5, should be non-eventful.  to make room for
this monsters should be able to attack (and kill) each other to gain
experience (this can have many side effects).  one obvious patch would
be that monsters that are killed by other monsters should rarely leave
inventories or corpses.  one consequence of this would be that genociding
cats, for example, would correctly wipe out all cats (of all ages).

